.page ln 1 make symbolic links

# SYNOPSIS
*ln* *-s* [*-f*] _TARGET_ _LINKNAME_
*ln* *-s* [*-f*] _TARGET_ _DIRECTORY_

# DESCRIPTION
`ln` creates a symbolic link called _LINKNAME_ that points at _TARGET_. If the second operand is an existing directory the link is created inside it, named after the target. The filesystem of this system has no hard links, so `-s` is required and `ln` without it explains why it cannot comply.

# OPTIONS
@ *-s*
    Make a symbolic link.
@ *-f*
    Remove an existing file called _LINKNAME_ first.

# EXAMPLES
    ln -s /Hakurei/etc /tmp/etc-link
    ln -sf /bin/ls /tmp/dir

# EXIT STATUS
0, or 1 on failure.

# SEE ALSO
readlink(1), ls(1), realpath(1)
